Z||000015||artherd||09-25-2001||11:51 PM||||I really like the Turbo MR2s.  They're incredibly fast stock (and can be made just insane.)  As been said, the engine (and spirit of their drivers!!) is in the right place.<P>I envy their stock performance, build quality, new-car-ness, and *engine reliability!!!*<P>I've had the pleasure of driving a really sweet 95 turbo with some very nice grippy 17" wheels/tyres, and wow could she go!<P>I actually think my Formula could out-turn it however, the Mk2s remind me of Ferrari Testarosas in their handling attributes, only more unstable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I wouldn't at all mind owning one, and eventually I'm sure I will.   It will probally be a Lexus V8 swap into a worked over (legenthened?) Mk.II.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
